The provisions of this article shall not apply in the following instances:
(1) When any such minor is accompanied by his parent, guardian, or other adult person having the lawful care and custody of such minor;
(2) When the minor is upon an emergency errand directed by his parent, guardian, or other adult person 21 years of age or older having the lawful care and custody of the minor;
(3) When the minor is traveling directly from home to lawful employment or returning directly home from lawful employment during the prescribed period of time;
(4) When the minor is engaged in interstate and intrastate vehicular travel through the city with parental consent, and with no intent to stop or sojourn in the city;
(5) When the minor is enrolled in a valid home study program, as authorized by O.C.G.A. § 20-2-690, and has written consent from a parent or legal guardian to be outside the home;
(6) When the minor has graduated from high school;
(7) When the minor has written proof from school authorities that he is excused from school attendance at that particular time; or
(8) When the minor is participating in an approved school or study activity which requires the minor to be off school property.
(Ord. No. 560, § 2, 10-19-2000)

564:
It shall be unlawful for any person within the city, in any manner for exhibition or display, to:
(1) Place or cause to be placed any word, figure, mark, picture, design, drawing, or any advertisement of any nature upon any flag, standard, colors, or ensign of the United States of America;
(2) Expose or cause to be exposed to public view any such flag, standard, colors, or ensign, upon which shall have been printed, painted, or otherwise placed, or to which shall be attached, appended, affixed, or annexed, any word, figure, mark, picture, design, drawing, or any advertisement of any nature;
(3) Within the city, manufacture, sell, expose for sale or to public view, or give away or have in his possession for sale or to be given away, or for use for any purpose, any article or substance being an article of merchandise or a receptacle for merchandise, or article or thing for carrying or transporting merchandise, upon which shall have been printed, or otherwise placed as a representation of, any such flag, standard, colors, or ensign, to advertise, call attention to, decorate, mark, or distinguish the article or substance on which so placed;
(4) Within the city, use such flag, standard, colors, or ensign as a receptacle for receiving, holding, carrying, or delivering anything; or
(5) Within the city, knowingly cast contempt upon by publicly mutilating, defacing, defiling, burning, or trampling upon any such flag, standard, colors, or ensign.
(Ord. No. 151-A)
